    {
      "body": "Do you have a concrete example? At least when I tried the example in https://numpy.org/devdocs/reference/generated/numpy.ndarray.nbytes.html, the result of `sys.getsizeof` is actually larger than the result of `.nbytes`, so the existing estimate is more conservative.",
      "created_at": "2026-07-07T16:35:18Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/47893#issuecomment-4906095895",
      "id": 4906095895,
      "updated_at": "2026-07-07T16:35:18Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "DarkLight1337"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "This pull request has merge conflicts that must be resolved before it can be\nmerged. Please rebase the PR, @damienlaine.\n\nhttps://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/collaborating-with-pull-requests/working-with-forks/syncing-a-fork\n",
      "created_at": "2026-09-21T19:42:02Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/47893#issuecomment-5766438283",
      "id": 5766438283,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-21T19:42:02Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "mergify[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "You're right. `sys.getsizeof` only undercounts views (`np.zeros(32000, np.float32)[:16000]`: 112 vs 64000 bytes), and I assumed Voxtral realtime frames reached the cache as views since they're slices. Checked on current main: the processor hands the cache a Tensor, on both sides of the IPC, and the size is counted right. No concrete case left, closing.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-25T12:38:57Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/47893#issuecomment-6397740947",
      "id": 6397740947,
